## Decision: which projects this gates

Made by the developer when transcript publishing was planned.

**Double Diaper Dungeon is cleared and does not wait on this.** Its subject
matter is its own game; no third party appears in it, and the pattern scan
agrees with that reading. Publishing it needs no audit and no stripping system.

**The concern is specific to projects whose subject matter is other people.**
neocities-modernization is the example that raised this issue and remains the
case that needs it: it processes posts from the fediverse and bluesky, so other
people's names and handles arrive in the transcripts as ordinary content rather
than as accidents.

So this is not a gate on the publishing system. It is a gate on *a particular
project publishing*, and the two must not be confused — building the first as
though it required the second would stop work that has no reason to wait.

What issue 030 should carry, then, is not "settle this first" but "a project
publishes only once somebody has said it may", with Double Diaper Dungeon
already having been said of.
